title ores.service Component

set namespaceSeparator ::

namespace ores #F2F2F2 {
    namespace service #F2F2F2 {
        enum error_code {
            unauthorized
            token_expired
            forbidden
            bad_request
        }
        namespace config #F2F2F2 {
            class standard_options <<struct>> {
                +logging : optional<ores::logging::logging_options>
                +nats : ores::nats::config::nats_options
                +database : ores::database::database_options
            }
            class standard_service_options {
            }
        }
        namespace messaging #F2F2F2 {
            class workflow_step_context <<struct>> {
                +step_id : string
                +instance_id : string
                +tenant_id : string
                +nats : ores::nats::service::client*
            }
            class cached_step_result <<struct>> {
                +result_json : string
                +error_message : string
                +log : vector<ores::workflow::messaging::step_log_entry>
            }
        }
        namespace service #F2F2F2 {
            enum exit_code {
                ok
                general_error
                config_error
                db_connection_failed
                nats_connection_failed
                startup_timeout
                auth_error
            }
            class heartbeat_publisher {
                -service_name_ : string
                -instance_id_ : string
                -version_ : string
                -nats_ : ores::nats::service::client&
                -interval_seconds_ : uint32_t
            }
            class host_runner_options <<struct>> {
                +failure_message : string_view
            }
        }
    }
}

' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

' The automated pass reads types and their data members. It arrives with the
' fields of a struct and no API, an empty box for a class whose content is
' methods, and nothing at all for a facet of free functions. The blocks below
' fill those in and record the one relationship the parser cannot infer.
'
' Each block names its class fully qualified rather than reopening a namespace,
' because reopening one that already holds classes crashes this PlantUML
' version. Redeclaring a class merges the members below into the box the
' automated pass drew, so a refresh keeps both.

class ores::service::config::standard_service_options {
    {static} +make_options_description(log_file : const string&, extra_options : const options_description&) : options_description
    {static} +parse(od : const options_description&, arguments : const vector<string>&, app_name : const string&) : variables_map
    {static} +read_options(vm : const variables_map&) : standard_options
    {static} +wants_help(vm : const variables_map&) : bool
    {static} +wants_version(vm : const variables_map&) : bool
}
note right of "ores::service::config::standard_service_options"
The one place a domain service reads its shared options.
It is also the single call site for
nats_configuration::register_shared_domain().
end note

class ores::service::service::heartbeat_publisher {
    +heartbeat_publisher(service_name : string, version : string, nats : client&, interval_seconds : uint32_t)
    +run() : awaitable<void>
}
note right of "ores::service::service::heartbeat_publisher"
A domain service co-spawns it from the runner's on_started
hook. It mints a per-process instance id at construction,
publishes once immediately and then on the interval, and
exits when the io_context stops. A failed publish is logged
and does not stop the loop.
end note

class ores::service::messaging::workflow_step_context {
    {static} +from_message(nats : client&, msg : const message&) : optional<workflow_step_context>
    +complete(result_json : const string&) : void
    +warn(result_json : const string&, log : const vector<step_log_entry>&) : void
    +fail(error_msg : const string&, log : const vector<step_log_entry>&) : void
}
note right of "ores::service::messaging::workflow_step_context"
from_message returns nothing unless the message carries
X-Workflow-Step-Id, which is how a handler chooses the
workflow path. All three publishers end in one private
publish() of a step_completed_event.
end note

note as OresServiceLifecycle
    Free functions in ores::service::service:
    run(io_ctx, nats, ctx, name, register_fn, on_started, on_shutdown) : awaitable<void>
    run(io_ctx, nats, name, register_fn, on_started, on_shutdown) : awaitable<void>
    run_signing(io_ctx, nats, ctx, name, jwt_private_key, register_fn, on_started, on_shutdown) : awaitable<void>
    The standard service lifecycle: signal handling, JWKS key
    fetch with exponential backoff, verifier or signer creation,
    registration, readiness, and a graceful drain. The database
    overload scopes every request from the JWT; the signing
    overload mints its own tokens for IAM; all three share one
    registration-and-drain tail.
end note

note as OresServiceHostRunner
    Free functions in ores::service::service:
    run_host_async(args, std_output, error_output, io_ctx, lg, opts, Parser, Application) : awaitable<int>
    run_host_sync(args, std_output, error_output, lg, early_exit, run_application, opts, Parser) : int
    The host envelope every service and tool shares: parse the
    arguments, start the logging lifecycle, log the run, run the
    application, and log and rethrow a failure. opts is taken by
    value because an awaitable starts lazily and would otherwise
    outlive the caller's frame.
end note

note as OresServiceRequestContext
    Free function in ores::service::service:
    make_request_context(base_ctx, msg, verifier) : expected<context, error_code>
    Validates the Bearer JWT in the message headers and returns
    a context scoped to its tenant, party and roles, narrowed by
    the X-Workspace-Id and X-Workspace-Resolution headers. With
    no verifier the base context is returned unchanged.
    X-Delegated-Authorization is checked before Authorization,
    and an expired delegated token is a hard reject.
end note

note as OresServiceMessaging
    Free functions and values in ores::service::messaging:
    log_handler_entry(lg, msg) : string
    has_permission(ctx, required_permission) : bool
    stamp(obj, ctx, change_reason) : void
    delegated_actor(ctx) : const string&
    reply(nats, msg, resp) : void
    error_reply(nats, msg, code) : void
    decode(msg) : optional<Req>
    change_reasons::new_record
    change_reasons::update
    is_workflow_command(msg) : bool
    extract_workflow_header(msg, header_name) : string
    publish_step_completion(...) : void
    check_step_idempotency(nats, step_id) : optional<cached_step_result>
    The handler surface a domain service writes against. stamp()
    matches fields by name, so it overwrites any party_id-named
    field from the context; a type whose party_id is a target
    rather than an ownership boundary needs its own stamp.
end note

note as OresServiceSystemdNotify
    Free function in ores::service::service:
    notify_systemd_ready() noexcept
    Writes READY=1 to the AF_UNIX datagram socket named by
    $NOTIFY_SOCKET, implementing sd_notify(3)'s wire protocol
    rather than linking libsystemd. A no-op when the variable is
    unset, and it never throws.
end note

